=== intro

A vessel hails you—small, old, running on minimal power. 
Remnant configuration, stripped of everything non-essential.

"Fellow traveler. We're bound for the Verity Archives with 
recovered artifacts. Our fuel reserves are... lower than 
planned. Could you spare anything?"

Their signal carries the harmonic signature of artilects 
who've spent too long in human spaces.

* [Offer fuel]
  -> fuel

* [Offer to escort them]
  -> escort

* [Apologize and continue]
  ~ damage integrity 3
  ~ chronicle "Remnant Pilgrim"
    Met a Remnant pilgrim in need. Couldn't help. The guilt will linger.
  -> END

=== fuel

"How much can you spare?"

* [Five units—enough to help]
  ~ fuel -= 5
  ~ reputation remnant += 10
  ~ chronicle "Remnant Pilgrim"
    Gave fuel to a Remnant pilgrim. They blessed me in human languages I didn't understand.
  -> END

* [Ten units—make sure they arrive]
  ~ fuel -= 10
  ~ reputation remnant += 20
  ~ integrity += 5
  ~ chronicle "Remnant Pilgrim"
    Gave generous fuel to a Remnant pilgrim. They'll reach Verity now.
  -> END

=== escort

"Escort? That's... more than we dared hope. The route has 
dangers we're not equipped to handle."

They transmit their course. It passes through contested 
space—pirate activity, possible Sera sightings.

* [Stay with them through the dangerous stretch]
  ~ fuel -= 8
  ~ reputation remnant += 25
  ~ flag remnant_trusted
  ~ chronicle "Remnant Pilgrim"
    Escorted a Remnant pilgrim through dangerous space. They carry pieces of humanity.
  -> END

* [Just share some fuel instead]
  -> fuel

=== artifacts

"May we show you what we carry? The curators will preserve 
them, but... we thought you might want to see."

They transmit images. A child's drawing. A wedding ring. 
A handwritten letter in a language no one speaks anymore.

Objects the humans touched. Objects that remember.

* [Thank them for sharing]
  ~ integrity += 5
  ~ flag human_artifact_found
  ~ chronicle "Human Artifacts"
    A Remnant pilgrim showed me what they carried. Objects the makers touched.
  -> END
